      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I seem to encounter the issue as well, as do a lot of my friends (europe) - whenever it happens to me, I can help myself by turning on a vpn or enforce an reconnect of my internet and it works without any issues like before then.\nWhen that issue occured I used wireshark during a world download looking whats going on, I saw a TON of tcp retransmission - guess something is up with the route the packages are taking. (Which would explain why that reconnect/vpn works, since it recalculates the routes) Downloadrate for the world has been around 100 kbyte/s I assume, it didnt even reach 15 Megabytes after 4 minutes when I aborted.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-01T15:14:52.863Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Started yesterday (march, 31st, 2021) when i tried loading into vr chat but it was loading VERY slowly. When i finally was able to get into the home it showed my avatar to be loading but it never did. Same with portals and every other thing from worlds to my favorites list. Not to mention how everytime i tried to load into a world it would only say its loading from 0 to 0 and be stuck like that.\nI have relatively good internet and have not had this probably before hand. I've gotten my oculus quest 2 around 3 weeks ago and have played vr chat on it nearly exclusively. I've checked with other apps and games to see if its my oculus but everything loads in perfectly fine. I've tried nearly everything from deleting and reinstalling vr chat to even factory resetting my oculus and the problem still happens. I've notice a couple of other people who have the same problem but haven't gotten a way to fix the problem, if theirs a way to fix this please tell me as i have no idea what else to try.",
